    "done_when": "In maps/jt-60sa/maps/magnetics.json (the live development bundle, reached through the worktree's maps symlink), each of the 26 loop rules for loops 1-6 and 8-27 targets its type-6 entry in the 53-loop store, the entry whose indices_differential is [7, L], in place of loop L's type-1 entry. Each carries channel_factor -1, because that entry stores -raw_L. Loops 12-27 are corpus-validated, with evidence citing the loop-reference fits in docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-loop-reference-rca.html. Loops 1-6 and 8-11 stay source-only, with the reason that they track only on E100642. Loop 7's rule is unchanged. The rules are rewritten by a script kept with the evidence, never by hand. The prior file is copied first to maps/jt-60sa/superseded/pre-differential-loops/maps/magnetics.json, and the fragment records both sha256s. In imas_ambix/data/cocos_convention.py, the absolute-loop selector keeps a proven rule only when its target entry carries no indices_differential, so after the retarget the sign cohort still reads loop 7 alone, and scripts/jt60sa_sign_cohort.py still reports COCOS (1, 2, 11, 12). New tests in tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py pin the retarget: every loop rule other than loop 7 resolves to a type-6 entry naming [7, L], and the corpus-validated loops are 7 and 12-27. New tests in tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py pin the selector against a corpus-validated differential rule. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH unset, uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_jt60sa_signal_maps.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_unit_audit.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/gs/test_operator_differential_loops.py tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py exits 0 and the cohort script exits 0, each captured once to a log with the revision and command on its first lines, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. A landing fragment is written to the fragment path.",
